    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **254 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes owner responses include a `displayName` field formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nTwo edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping on `toOwnerDto` that computes the field from the stored entity:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n           expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nSince `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (and the GET responder) already map the persisted `Owner` through `OwnerMapper`, the display name is derived from the *stored* names, exactly as specified. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` passes, as does the entire existing suite.",
